WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.460
These all look like putting money in. Which one do I press?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.857
Start with what you're holding.

00:00:10.857 --> 00:00:13.863
Money in your bank, coins you already have somewhere else,

00:00:13.863 --> 00:00:16.610
or a balance in another account on the same platform.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.320
Each one takes a different route.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.559
A fiat deposit usually adds a cash balance to your account.

00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:39.149
Buying crypto directly means you pay and receive a crypto asset.

00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:42.346
Some platforms support bank or card channels, some don't,

00:00:42.346 --> 00:00:43.860
and fees and limits differ.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.482
If you already hold crypto, you can deposit it using a supported coin and network.

00:01:04.482 --> 00:01:07.682
An internal transfer just moves balance between your accounts.

00:01:07.682 --> 00:01:11.760
It's usually not an on-chain transfer. Check where the balance will land first.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.128
Some platforms also offer trading between users.

00:01:27.128 --> 00:01:31.864
That's not another name for a bank transfer. Never pay off-platform in private,

00:01:31.864 --> 00:01:35.342
never use funds of unknown origin or third-party payments.

00:01:35.342 --> 00:01:37.320
If it's unclear, don't do it yet.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.290
No. They're different channels.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:45.938
Right.

00:01:45.938 --> 00:01:50.630
Look at the asset first, then the route, and finally check what actually arrived.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:01.950
BTC/USDT: does that slash mean you buy two coins? Next: your first spot trade.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.740
Understand first, then act.
